{
 "about": "RAG retrieval evaluation set (scripts/eval_rag.py, tests/test_rag_eval.py). Each case: the user question as typed in chat; `sources` = acceptable source ids (a hit = any of them retrieved); `terms` = optional strings of which at least one must appear in the packed passages; `expect_empty` = nothing in the corpus answers it, so retrieval should return no passages. Pathway is inferred exactly as chat does (rag_service.infer_pathway). `tags` group cases in the report: core (one per covered topic), lay (everyday wording), fact (a specific number or criterion must appear), cross (spans two pathways), holdout (lay questions written by a separate agent that never saw app.rag.lexicon, so they measure the expansion fairly), off_topic and near_miss (health-sounding but not covered; must abstain).",
